---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Agentic OS · Multi-Agent Systems Consulting",
  "serviceType": "AI Agent Systems Consulting",
  "provider": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pravine Manivannan", "url": "https://pravinemani.com/" },
  "areaServed": "Worldwide",
  "description": "Multi-agent orchestration systems, sub-agent design, concurrent-agent evals, and the trade-off analysis on when more agents stop being a win.",
  "url": "https://pravinemani.com/services/agentic-os/"
};
---

<Base title="Agentic OS · Multi-Agent Systems Consulting · Pravine Mani" description="Multi-agent orchestration, sub-agent design, concurrent-agent evals, and the trade-off analysis on when more agents stop being a win. Toronto consultancy." jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/services/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">services</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <span class="you">agentic os</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Agentic OS.<br><span class="accent">Multi-agent systems that don't drift.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">When a single agent is not enough and three are already too many. Multi-agent orchestration with sub-agent design, inter-agent state, concurrent-execution evaluation, and a concrete answer to <em>"what breaks past five concurrent agents?"</em> built from a year of research.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <span class="cta-btn cta-btn-secondary" style="cursor: default; opacity: 0.7;">Not bookable yet</span>
    <a href="/services/" class="cta-btn secondary">← Back to all services</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-cta reveal" style="border-color: #ffd84a; margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #ffd84a; margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;">▍ IN DEVELOPMENT · COMING SOON</p>
    <p style="font-size: 17px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 12px;">Agentic OS is not bookable yet. I am productizing internal R&amp;D into client engagements through Q3 2026.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0;">Below is what the service will cover when it opens. If you are already running multi-agent systems and uncovering interesting failure modes, I would like to hear what you are building. <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Send me a note →</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="vert-grid">

    <article class="vert-card" id="builds">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">01</span><h2>Multi-agent builds</h2></div>
      <p>End-to-end agent systems with multiple specialized workers, an orchestrator, an evaluator, and structured outputs at every boundary. Built on Claude + MCP, runs on Vercel / Supabase / Modal where it fits.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Orchestrator / worker / evaluator patterns</li>
        <li>Inter-agent state via shared filesystem or vector store</li>
        <li>Cost ceilings per task + per user</li>
        <li>Production observability via Langfuse or Helicone</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="orchestration">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">02</span><h2>Orchestration audit</h2></div>
      <p>You have agents in production. They mostly work. Occasionally they loop. Occasionally they exceed budget. This audit identifies the orchestration bug before the next demo.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Tool-use graph review (what calls what, when)</li>
        <li>Failure mode taxonomy from real production logs</li>
        <li>Hard ceilings + fallback paths recommendations</li>
        <li>Written report + 30-day fix plan</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="subagents">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">03</span><h2>Sub-agent design</h2></div>
      <p>When to spawn a sub-agent versus an in-process tool call versus a separate process. The decision tree most teams get wrong. Token cost versus latency versus isolation, with the trade-off math made explicit.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Sub-agent boundary recommendations per workflow</li>
        <li>Context-isolation patterns for parallel work</li>
        <li>Sync vs async fan-out</li>
        <li>The "when not to fan out" rules nobody documents</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="evals">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">04</span><h2>Concurrent-agent evals</h2></div>
      <p>Single-agent evaluation suites are well-understood. Multi-agent ones are not. A real harness for the question every team should be asking before shipping: does this system still work with five concurrent agents under load?</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Concurrent-execution test harness</li>
        <li>Race-condition + ordering-violation detection</li>
        <li>Cost regression alerts</li>
        <li>CI integration via Promptfoo or custom runner</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-cta reveal" style="border-color: #ffd84a;">
    <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: #ffd84a; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 14px;">▍ EARLY-COLLABORATOR LIST · Q3 2026 LAUNCH</p>
    <h2 style="color: var(--text-primary);">Already running multi-agent systems at scale?<br><span style="color: #ffd84a;">I would like to talk before this opens.</span></h2>
    <p>Skip the form and send what you are building. Token bills, orchestration diagrams, evaluation failures. The first five early-collaborator engagements are priced as design partnerships rather than standard consulting.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content: center;">
      <a href="/contact/" class="cta-btn">Tell me what you're building →</a>
      <a href="/services/ai/" class="cta-btn secondary">See standard AI workflows</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
